Description: Homelab service/config backup client built on borg
 Client-side backup tool that pushes encrypted per-host borg archives to
 a centralized backup server over SSH, driven by a per-host config in
 /etc/homelab/borgbackup/ and run under systemd. Intended to let an
 administrator restore a homelab service's config (/etc/homelab/*) or an
 entire server to a point in time after a disaster; not a user-data
 backup tool. Run `homelab-borgbackup configure` after installing this
 package to set up config and encryption; SSH trust to the backup server
 is completed by an administrator running `enroll` on the
 homelab-borg-service-backup-server package, using this client's printed
 public key.
